        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-30T19:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of the new flag, I think we can just say that if `init` fails the encoder should not take ownership of the memory. In that case the stored pointers could be cleared before returning so `vpx_codec_destroy` is a noop.",
      "revId": "b1773e95b122c8e00cb8379f74057f4dacf4adf6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
